[38;2;124;124;124mLet me double-check the argument for $n \geq 2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe cohomology ring of $\mathbb{C}P^n$ is $\mathbb{Z}[\alpha]/(\alpha^{n+1})$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwith $|\alpha| = 2$. The top class is $\alpha^n \in H^{2n}(\mathbb{C}P^n)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor any map $f: S^{2n} \to \mathbb{C}P^n$, the induced map on cohomology is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mring homomorphism:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$f^*: H^*(\mathbb{C}P^n) \to H^*(S^{2n})$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $f^*$ is a ring homomorphism, $f^*(\alpha^n) = (f^*(\alpha))^n$.[0m

