[38;2;124;124;124m\geq 2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor $n = 1$: $\mathbb{C}P^1 \cong S^2$, and the identity map $S^2 \to \mathbb{C}[0m[38;2;124;124;124mP^1$ induces an isomorphism on $H^2$. So $n = 1$ works.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore, the answer is $n = 1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me also verify: is the ring homomorphism argument valid? Yes, the induced [0m
